    "q-95282": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95282",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $y=3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we recall the results for the derivatives of the basic reciprocal hyperbolic functions:\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)^{′}=-{csch}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the given function using these results, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-(-{csch}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x-3\\operatorname{coth}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
