    "q-95577": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95577",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=2{sech}^{2}⁡x.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=2{g}^{2},\\,g=\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=4g,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =4g(-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x) \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)(-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x) \\\\  & =-4{sech}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-95577-a",
