    "q-95566": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95566",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=-2\\operatorname{csch}⁡(1-4x).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=-2\\operatorname{csch}⁡g,\\,g=1-4x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=2\\operatorname{csch}⁡g\\operatorname{coth}⁡g,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=-4.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =2\\operatorname{csch}⁡g\\operatorname{coth}⁡g\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-8\\operatorname{csch}⁡g\\operatorname{coth}⁡g \\\\  & =-8\\operatorname{csch}⁡(1-4x)\\operatorname{coth}⁡(1-4x).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
