    "q-95570": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95570",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=\\operatorname{coth}⁡({x}^{2}-1).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=\\operatorname{coth}⁡g,\\,g={x}^{2}-1\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=-{csch}^{2}⁡g,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=2x.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =-{csch}^{2}⁡g\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =-2x{csch}^{2}⁡g \\\\  & =-2x{csch}^{2}⁡({x}^{2}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-95570-a",
