    "q-95580": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95580",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $f(x)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{csch}⁡4x,$ then ${f}^{′}(x)=2x\\operatorname{csch}⁡4x\\cdot g(x).$ What is $g(x)?$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)={x}^{2}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{csch}⁡4x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={({x}^{2})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{csch}⁡4x+{x}^{2}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{csch}⁡4x)}^{′} \\\\  & =2x\\cdot \\operatorname{csch}⁡4x+{x}^{2}\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{csch}⁡4x\\operatorname{coth}⁡4x) \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{csch}⁡4x-4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{csch}⁡4x\\operatorname{coth}⁡4x \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{csch}⁡4x\\cdot {{(1-2x\\operatorname{coth}⁡4x)}_{⏟}}_{g(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)=1-2x\\operatorname{coth}⁡4x.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
