    "q-95588": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95588",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=-3x{csch}^{2}⁡x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=-3x$ and $v(x)={csch}^{2}⁡x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(-3x)}^{′}\\cdot {csch}^{2}⁡x+(-3x)\\cdot {({csch}^{2}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {csch}^{2}⁡x-3x\\cdot (2\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =-3{csch}^{2}⁡x+6x{csch}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x \\\\  & =3{csch}^{2}⁡x(2x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
