    "q-95585": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95585",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=2{x}^{3}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{coth}⁡x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(2{x}^{3})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{coth}⁡x+2{x}^{3}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{coth}⁡x+2{x}^{3}\\cdot (-{csch}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-2{x}^{3}{csch}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}(3\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-x{csch}^{2}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
