      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=2x\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=2x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(2x)}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}+2x\\cdot {(\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2})}^{′} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}+2x\\cdot (-2x{csch}^{2}⁡{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}-4{x}^{2}{csch}^{2}⁡{x}^{2} \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}-2{x}^{2}{csch}^{2}⁡{x}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
