    "q-95285": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95285",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=x\\operatorname{sech}⁡3x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{sech}⁡3x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =(x)^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{sech}⁡3x+x\\cdot (\\operatorname{sech}⁡3x)^{′} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\operatorname{sech}⁡3x+x\\cdot (-3\\operatorname{sech}⁡3x\\cdot \\operatorname{tanh}⁡3x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sech}⁡3x-3x\\operatorname{sech}⁡3x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡3x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sech}⁡3x(1-3x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡3x)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
