    "q-95893": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95893",
      "name": "Question 16",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x},$ then ${f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{g(x)}{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}.$ What is $g(x)?$",
      "worked_solution": "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{csch}⁡x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′}}{{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x})}{{ln}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\overset{g(x)}{\\overset{⏞}{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+1)}}}{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)=\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+1).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-95893-a",
