    "q-95287": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95287",
      "name": "Question 17",
      "problem": "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{csch}⁡x$ and $v(x)=2{x}^{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot 2{x}^{2}-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\cdot (2{x}^{2})^{′}}{(2{x}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-4x\\operatorname{csch}⁡x}{4{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+2)}{4{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+2)}{2{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
