    "q-95889": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95889",
      "name": "Question 19",
      "problem": "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x}.$",
      "worked_solution": "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)={x}^{2}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{({x}^{2})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{sech}⁡2x-{x}^{2}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x)}^{′}}{{(\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x-{x}^{2}(-2\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡2x)}{{sech}^{2}⁡2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x(1+x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡2x)}{{sech}^{2}⁡2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x(1+x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡2x)}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-95889-a",
              "type": "math",
