    "q-95896": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95896",
      "name": "Question 20",
      "problem": "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x}{{3}^{x}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{csch}⁡x$ and $v(x)={3}^{x}.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)}^{′}\\cdot {3}^{x}-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\cdot {({3}^{x})}^{′}}{{({3}^{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)\\cdot {3}^{x}-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\cdot ({3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)}{{3}^{2x}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{3}^{x}\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)}{{3}^{2x}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)}{{3}^{x}}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
